#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction to TEM, a Qiskit Function by Algorithmiq, to compute estimations with software post-processing error mitigation using tensor networks."
msgstr "Panimula sa TEM, isang Qiskit Function ng Algorithmiq, para sa pagkalkula ng mga estimasyon gamit ang software post-processing error mitigation na gumagamit ng tensor networks."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate a kicked Ising model with the TEM function"
msgstr "Simulate ang isang kicked Ising model gamit ang TEM function"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore Floquet, linestyles */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore Floquet, linestyles */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithmiq's Tensor-network Error Mitigation (TEM) method is a hybrid quantum-classical algorithm designed for performing noise mitigation entirely within the classical post-processing stage. With TEM, the user can compute observables' expectation values,  mitigating the inevitable noise-induced errors that occur on quantum hardware with increased accuracy and cost efficiency, making it a highly attractive option for quantum researchers and industry practitioners alike.\n"
msgstr "Ang Tensor-network Error Mitigation (TEM) method ng Algorithmiq ay isang hybrid quantum-classical algorithm na dinisenyo para sa pagsasagawa ng noise mitigation nang buo sa loob ng classical post-processing stage. Gamit ang TEM, maaaring kalkulahin ng user ang mga expectation value ng observables, na mitigating ang hindi maiwasang noise-induced errors na nangyayari sa quantum hardware nang may mas mataas na katumpakan at cost efficiency, na ginagawa itong isang napaka-kaakit-akit na opsyon para sa mga quantum researcher at industry practitioner.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial demonstrates how TEM can obtain meaningful results for a quantum system's dynamics, which would be inaccessible without error mitigation and which require substantially more quantum resources if other error mitigation methods such as PEC and ZNE are used.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng tutorial na ito kung paano nakakakuha ang TEM ng makabuluhang resulta para sa dynamics ng isang quantum system, na hindi maaabot nang wala ang error mitigation at nangangailangan ng mas maraming quantum resources kung gagamit ng ibang error mitigation methods tulad ng PEC at ZNE.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Usage estimate: This notebook uses approximately 10 QPU minutes on Heron r3 devices. The runtime can depend substantially on the chosen device. Per-section usage estimates can be found below.*\n"
msgstr "*Tinantyang paggamit: Gumagamit ang notebook na ito ng humigit-kumulang 10 QPU minutes sa Heron r3 devices. Maaaring malaki ang pagkakaiba ng runtime depende sa piniling device. Ang tinantyang paggamit bawat seksyon ay nasa ibaba.*\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run error-mitigated many-body physics experiments with the TEM function {#run-error-mitigated-many-body-physics-experiments-with-the-tem-function}"
msgstr "Magpatakbo ng error-mitigated many-body physics experiments gamit ang TEM function {#run-error-mitigated-many-body-physics-experiments-with-the-tem-function}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial is based on the following reference: [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9). This reference discusses a real simulation on quantum hardware of up to 91 qubits. In this tutorial, we recreate a similar simulation on a smaller circuit size.\n"
msgstr "Ang tutorial na ito ay batay sa sumusunod na sanggunian: [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9). Tinatalakay ng sangguniang ito ang isang tunay na simulation sa quantum hardware ng hanggang 91 qubits. Sa tutorial na ito, muling ginagawa namin ang isang katulad na simulation sa mas maliit na laki ng circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The kicked Ising model corresponds to the usual Ising model:\n"
msgstr "Ang kicked Ising model ay katumbas ng karaniwang Ising model:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$ \\hat{H}_{\\text{I}} = J \\sum_{n=0}^{N-2} \\hat{Z}_n \\hat{Z}_{n+1} + h \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{Z}_n $$\n"
msgstr "$$ \\hat{H}_{\\text{I}} = J \\sum_{n=0}^{N-2} \\hat{Z}_n \\hat{Z}_{n+1} + h \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{Z}_n $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "to which is applied a transverse kick:\n"
msgstr "kung saan inilalapat ang isang transverse kick:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$ \\hat{H}_{K} = b \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{X}_n $$\n"
msgstr "$$ \\hat{H}_{K} = b \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} \\hat{X}_n $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The goal is to simulate the dynamics of a state under the transverse kicked Ising Hamiltonian, whose time evolution can be implemented by a Floquet unitary $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}} = e^{-i \\hat{H}_K} e^{-i \\hat{H}_I} $. The initial state to evolve is the one in which the first qubit is in the state $|+\\rangle$, while the others are paired up and set in the Bell state $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$.\n"
msgstr "Ang layunin ay i-simulate ang dynamics ng isang estado sa ilalim ng transverse kicked Ising Hamiltonian, na ang time evolution ay maaaring ipatupad ng isang Floquet unitary $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}} = e^{-i \\hat{H}_K} e^{-i \\hat{H}_I}$. Ang initial state na ie-evolve ay ang isa kung saan ang unang qubit ay nasa estado $|+\\rangle$, habang ang iba ay pinagsamasama at nakatakda sa Bell state $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The quantity we want to observe is the correlation function. The [reference paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) discusses how this quantity can be rewritten as an $\\hat{X}$ Pauli operator on the $n^{th}$ qubit.\n"
"After a number of physical time steps $t$, we compute the value of the Pauli operator $\\hat{X}_{n=t}$.\n"
"Depending on the system's parameters, the value of this observable is equal to a value that can be computed exactly, or only simulated through approximate methods. Specifically, for $|J|=|b|=\\pi/4$ it is equal to $[\\cos(2h)]^t$, which is the value we will use to benchmark the results of this tutorial. Furthermore, at a given time step $t$, $\\langle\\hat{X}_{n\\neq t}\\rangle$ is zero. For details to obtain these values, and for comparison with approximate classical simulation results outside of these parameters, see [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang dami na nais nating obserbahan ay ang correlation function. Tinatalakay ng [reference paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9) kung paano maaaring isulat muli ang daming ito bilang isang $\\hat{X}$ Pauli operator sa $n^{th}$ qubit.\n"
"Pagkatapos ng ilang physical time steps $t$, kinakalkula namin ang halaga ng Pauli operator $\\hat{X}_{n=t}$.\n"
"Depende sa mga parameter ng system, ang halaga ng observable na ito ay katumbas ng isang halagang maaaring kalkulahin nang eksakto, o simulation lamang sa pamamagitan ng mga approximate method. Specifically, para sa $|J|=|b|=\\pi/4$ ito ay katumbas ng $[\\cos(2h)]^t$, na siyang halagang gagamitin namin para sa benchmarking ng mga resulta ng tutorial na ito. Bukod dito, sa isang ibinigay na time step $t$, ang $\\langle\\hat{X}_{n\\neq t}\\rangle$ ay zero. Para sa mga detalye sa pagkuha ng mga halagang ito, at para sa paghahambing sa mga approximate classical simulation results sa labas ng mga parameter na ito, tingnan ang [L. E. Fischer et al., Nat. Phys. (2026)](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-025-03144-9).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEM works by first characterizing the noise for each unique layer of two-qubit gates in the circuit, as well as characterizing the readout error. Then, the circuit is executed on the quantum machine. Finally, the tensor network error mitigation is performed on the classical resources in IBM Cloud&reg; and the mitigated value is returned. In this example, the circuit has two unique layers to characterize.\n"
msgstr "Gumagana ang TEM sa pamamagitan ng unang pag-characterize ng noise para sa bawat natatanging layer ng two-qubit gates sa circuit, pati na rin ang pag-characterize ng readout error. Pagkatapos, ang circuit ay isinasagawa sa quantum machine. Sa wakas, ang tensor network error mitigation ay isinasagawa sa mga classical resources sa IBM Cloud&reg; at ibinabalik ang mitigated value. Sa halimbawang ito, ang circuit ay may dalawang natatanging layer na i-characterize.\n"

