msgstr "Bilang prerequisite, tiyakin na naka-install ang mga kinakailangang dependency.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error mitigation with TEM {#error-mitigation-with-tem}"
msgstr "Error mitigation gamit ang TEM {#error-mitigation-with-tem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We provide here a circuit that implements the kicked Ising model described above. The circuit is prepared as follows. First, there is a state preparation phase, in which the first qubit is in the state $|+\\rangle$, while the others are in Bell pairs $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$. This is followed by the brickwork structure that implements the unitary evolution $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}}$. The number of physical time steps correspond to $t/2$ circuit layers.\n"
"The following code downloads the two QASM files needed for this tutorial.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbibigay kami dito ng isang circuit na nagpapatupad ng kicked Ising model na inilarawan sa itaas. Ang circuit ay inihanda tulad ng sumusunod. Una, may isang state preparation phase, kung saan ang unang qubit ay nasa estado $|+\\rangle$, habang ang iba ay nasa Bell pairs $(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$. Sinusundan ito ng brickwork structure na nagpapatupad ng unitary evolution $\\hat{U}_{\\text{KI}}$. Ang bilang ng mga physical time steps ay katumbas ng $t/2$ circuit layers.\n"
"Dino-download ng sumusunod na code ang dalawang QASM file na kinakailangan para sa tutorial na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can visualize a small version of the circuit, with 12 qubits and six time steps:\n"
msgstr "Maaari naming i-visualize ang isang maliit na bersyon ng circuit, na may 12 qubits at anim na time steps:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem/extracted-outputs/381a4e25-bc9c-47d0-b9f1-172eb5516484-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem/extracted-outputs/381a4e25-bc9c-47d0-b9f1-172eb5516484-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, build the observable, $\\hat{X}_{n=t}$. It is constructed as a simple Pauli string with the order matching the one used by Qiskit:\n"
msgstr "Susunod, i-build ang observable, $\\hat{X}_{n=t}$. Ito ay itinayo bilang isang simpleng Pauli string na may order na tumutugma sa ginagamit ng Qiskit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In our small 12-qubit example, the observable looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Sa aming maliit na 12-qubit na halimbawa, ganito ang hitsura ng observable:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit Functions use PUBs as the way to collect the inputs. In our case, let's consider a single circuit and observable as our PUB:\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang Qiskit Functions ng PUBs bilang paraan ng pag-collect ng mga input. Sa aming kaso, isaalang-alang natin ang isang solong circuit at observable bilang aming PUB:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we get access to the TEM function. We first set up the required authentication to IBM Cloud and select a backend from the available devices. The token, available backends, and corresponding cloud resource names (CRN) can be obtained by logging in to your account on the [IBM Quantum Platform dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"
msgstr "Susunod, magkakakuha tayo ng access sa TEM function. Una, i-set up namin ang kinakailangang authentication sa IBM Cloud at pipili ng backend mula sa mga available na device. Ang token, available backends, at mga katumbas na cloud resource names (CRN) ay makukuha sa pamamagitan ng pag-log in sa iyong account sa [IBM Quantum Platform dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the TEM function from the [Qiskit Functions Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions):\n"
msgstr "I-load ang TEM function mula sa [Qiskit Functions Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now run an experiment on the kicked Ising circuit with error mitigation provided by TEM. Using default settings, TEM can be run in a simple way with an expected QPU runtime of around 2.5 minutes, depending on the QPU:\n"
msgstr "Maaari na tayong magpatakbo ng eksperimento sa kicked Ising circuit na may error mitigation na ibinibigay ng TEM. Gamit ang mga default na setting, maaaring patakbuhin ang TEM nang simple na may inaasahang QPU runtime na humigit-kumulang 2.5 minuto, depende sa QPU:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With default options, the TEM function runs three jobs on the quantum computer: noise learning, readout mitigation, and circuit sampling. The number of shots used by each of these can be changed in the options passed to the function. By default, these parameters are set to achieve a precision of 0.05 in the mitigated expectation values.\n"
"You can check the status of your job on the [IBM Quantum Platform dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/) or with:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga default na opsyon, nagpapatakbo ang TEM function ng tatlong trabaho sa quantum computer: noise learning, readout mitigation, at circuit sampling. Ang bilang ng shots na ginagamit ng bawat isa ay maaaring baguhin sa mga opsyon na ipinasa sa function. Bilang default, ang mga parameter na ito ay itinakda para makamit ang precision na 0.05 sa mga mitigated expectation values.\n"
"Maaari mong suriin ang status ng iyong trabaho sa [IBM Quantum Platform dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/) o gamit ang:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the status is `DONE`, we can check the raw and mitigated results. The `tem_evs` defined below are the expectation values of the requested observables, in this case just one observable, $\\langle \\hat X_{n=t}\\rangle$, and `tem_std` are the corresponding standard deviations.\n"
msgstr "Kapag ang status ay `DONE`, maaari na tayong suriin ang mga raw at mitigated na resulta. Ang `tem_evs` na tinukoy sa ibaba ay ang mga expectation value ng mga hiniling na observable, sa kasong ito ay isa lamang observable, ang $\\langle \\hat X_{n=t}\\rangle$, at ang `tem_std` ay ang mga katumbas na standard deviation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can also check how much quantum runtime was used for each call at [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com), or by inspecting the result metadata from the Python code.\n"
msgstr "Maaari rin nating suriin kung gaano karaming quantum runtime ang ginamit para sa bawat tawag sa [IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com), o sa pamamagitan ng pag-inspect ng result metadata mula sa Python code.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customize TEM parameters and advanced options {#customize-tem-parameters-and-advanced-options}"
msgstr "I-customize ang mga TEM parameter at advanced na opsyon {#customize-tem-parameters-and-advanced-options}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The TEM function provides several advanced options to customize your error mitigation workflow. These options allow you to control the precision, number of shots, noise learning strategies, and other parameters to better suit your experiment's requirements and available quantum resources.\n"
msgstr "Nagbibigay ang TEM function ng ilang advanced na opsyon para i-customize ang iyong error mitigation workflow. Ang mga opsyon na ito ay nagbibigay-daan sa iyo na kontrolin ang precision, bilang ng shots, mga estratehiya sa noise learning, at iba pang mga parameter upang mas maiangkop sa mga kinakailangan ng iyong eksperimento at mga available na quantum resources.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Common advanced options are:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga karaniwang advanced na opsyon ay:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`precision`**: Specify the target precision for the mitigated expectation values.\n"
msgstr "**`precision`**: Tukuyin ang target precision para sa mga mitigated expectation value.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`default_shots`**: Instead of `precision`, you can specify the number of shots used by the measurement job.\n"
msgstr "**`default_shots`**: Sa halip na `precision`, maaari mong tukuyin ang bilang ng shots na ginagamit ng measurement job.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`tem_max_bond_dimension`**: The maximum bond dimension used in the tensor network.\n"
msgstr "**`tem_max_bond_dimension`**: Ang maximum bond dimension na ginagamit sa tensor network.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`tem_compression_cutoff`**: The cutoff value to be used for the tensor network.\n"
msgstr "**`tem_compression_cutoff`**: Ang cutoff value na gagamitin para sa tensor network.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**noise learning options**: Configure how noise is characterized, such as the number of repetitions or specific calibration circuits.\n"
msgstr "**Mga opsyon sa noise learning**: I-configure kung paano nai-characterize ang noise, tulad ng bilang ng mga repetisyon o mga tiyak na calibration circuit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`private`**: Ensure that circuits and experiment results are private to you and disable multiple downloads of job results.\n"
msgstr "**`private`**: Tiyakin na ang mga circuit at resulta ng eksperimento ay pribado para sa iyo at i-disable ang maramihang pag-download ng mga resulta ng trabaho.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Refer to the [TEM documentation](/guides/algorithmiq-tem) or the [Qiskit Functions Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions) for a full list of supported options and their descriptions. You can adjust these parameters to balance between runtime, resource usage, and result accuracy.\n"
"You can pass these options as a dictionary to the `options` argument when running the TEM function:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sumangguni sa [dokumentasyon ng TEM](/guides/algorithmiq-tem) o sa [Qiskit Functions Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions) para sa kumpletong listahan ng mga sinusuportahang opsyon at ang kanilang mga paglalarawan. Maaari mong ayusin ang mga parameter na ito para balansehin ang runtime, paggamit ng resource, at katumpakan ng resulta.\n"
"Maaari mong ipasa ang mga opsyon na ito bilang isang dictionary sa `options` argument kapag nagpapatakbo ng TEM function:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Custom options for the noise learner can also be passed. They follow the definitions used in the `qiskit-ibm-runtime` [`NoiseLearnerOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-noise-learner-options):\n"
msgstr "Maaari ring ipasa ang mga custom na opsyon para sa noise learner. Sumusunod ang mga ito sa mga kahulugan na ginagamit sa `qiskit-ibm-runtime` [`NoiseLearnerOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-noise-learner-options):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Re-run the experiment with these custom options tuned to our circuit. The expected runtime is approximately four QPU minutes.\n"
msgstr "Ulit na patakbuhin ang eksperimento gamit ang mga custom na opsyon na ito na na-tune para sa aming circuit. Ang inaasahang runtime ay humigit-kumulang apat na QPU minuto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the job is not set as private, we can recover the result at a later point. To do so, save the job ID printed here and use `tem_job_custom = catalog.get_job_by_id(\"your-job-id\")`.\n"
msgstr "Kung ang trabaho ay hindi itinakda bilang pribado, maaari nating makuha ang resulta sa ibang pagkakataon. Para magawa iyon, i-save ang job ID na naka-print dito at gamitin ang `tem_job_custom = catalog.get_job_by_id(\"your-job-id\")`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now inspect the results and the metadata to get insight into the experiment:\n"
msgstr "Maaari na nating suriin ang mga resulta at ang metadata para makakuha ng pananaw sa eksperimento:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem/extracted-outputs/c3a2168d-98df-491e-a1f8-05de5684ab96-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/simulate-kicked-ising-tem/extracted-outputs/c3a2168d-98df-491e-a1f8-05de5684ab96-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we can check the impact of the custom options on QPU and classical runtime:\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, maaari nating suriin ang epekto ng mga custom na opsyon sa QPU at classical runtime:\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scale TEM to large circuits {#scale-tem-to-large-circuits}"
msgstr "I-scale ang TEM sa malalaking circuit {#scale-tem-to-large-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large circuits can, in principle, be run with the TEM function. However, it is important to be aware of the of the limitations of the classical resources, as TEM is executed on IBM Cloud runners with potentially very long run times. For extremely large circuits, contact the TEM support team at [qiskit_ibm@algorithmiq.fi](mailto:qiskit_ibm@algorithmiq.fi).\n"
msgstr "Ang malalaking circuit ay maaaring, sa prinsipyo, patakbuhin gamit ang TEM function. Gayunpaman, mahalagang maging mulat sa mga limitasyon ng mga classical resources, dahil ang TEM ay isinasagawa sa mga IBM Cloud runner na may potensyal na napakahaba ng run times. Para sa napakalalaking mga circuit, makipag-ugnayan sa TEM support team sa [qiskit_ibm@algorithmiq.fi](mailto:qiskit_ibm@algorithmiq.fi).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we run an example with a larger, utility-scale-sized 30-qubit circuit, optimizing the TEM parameters for speed rather than accuracy.\n"
msgstr "Dito tatakbuhin namin ang isang halimbawa na may mas malaki, utility-scale-sized na 30-qubit circuit, na ino-optimize ang mga TEM parameter para sa bilis kaysa sa katumpakan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's define some performance-oriented options:\n"
msgstr "Tukuyin natin ang ilang mga opsyon na nakatuon sa performance:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, run the experiment, get the result, and visualize it. This will take approximately 3.5 QPU minutes.\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, patakbuhin ang eksperimento, kunin ang resulta, at i-visualize ito. Tatagal ito ng humigit-kumulang 3.5 QPU minuto.\n"

